{"version": 2, "width": 80, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1793964750, "idle_time_limit": 1.0, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "config-init-file (gooze v1.5.1, goozels v0.4.1, go1.27.3)"}
[0.003224, "o", "# gooze.yaml: every key is optional; these are the defaults.\r\n# Reference: https://gooze.dev/docs/config/\r\noutput: .gooze-reports        # Directory where mutation reports are written.\r\nno_cache: false               # Disable incremental caching and force a full re-run.\r\nno_update_check: false        # Disable the check for a newer gooze release.\r\n\r\npaths:                        # Path selection settings.\r\n  exclude: []                 # Regular-expression patterns of files to skip (e.g. '^vendor/').\r\n\r\nrun:                          # Mutation run settings.\r\n  parallel: 1                 # Number of concurrent mutation workers.\r\n  mutation_timeout: 120       # Per-mutation timeout in seconds.\r\n  coverage_profile: ''        # Go coverage profile; mutations on uncovered lines are reported as not_covered without running tests.\r\n  diff: ''                    # Git ref to diff against; only lines changed since its merge base with HEAD are mutated. Requires git. Empty runs everything.\r\n  mutagens: []               "]
[0.004033, "o", " # Mutagens to run (arithmetic, boolean, numbers, comparison, logical, unary, bitwise, increment, assignment, branch, statement, loop); empty runs the default ones, all but branch, statement and loop.\r\n  workspace: overlay          # How mutants are built: overlay tests them in the project through go test -overlay, without copying it; deep-copy tests them in a per-worker copy of the project, for tests that build the project's code in a subprocess, read its source files or write next to themselves.\r\n  fail_fast: \"off\"            # When a run stops before testing every mutant: off tests them all; gate stops once a threshold can no longer be met; file skips the rest of a file once it can no longer meet threshold.file; first stops at the first surviving mutant. Untested mutants are tested by the next run.\r\n  go_cache: isolated          # Where the go command caches the builds of mutants: isolated keeps them in gooze's own cache (gooze/go-build in the user cache directory), which reads GOCACHE but never writes to "]
[0.004059, "o", "it; shared writes them to GOCACHE. Without Go 1.24, or with GOCACHEPROG set, gooze uses shared.\r\n  go_cache_size: 2048         # Size in MB that a run trims gooze's own Go build cache to when it ends, least recently used first; entries used in the last hour are kept.\r\n  go_cache_prewarm: false     # Build each package's tests once in GOCACHE before its mutants, so their dependencies are cached there. Only with go_cache: isolated.\r\n  test_flags: []              # Extra go test flags for the tests of every mutant, e.g. -short, -race, -tags=integration or -skip=TestSlow; values after =. Not -json, -count, -vet, -overlay, -c or -o, which gooze sets itself.\r\n\r\nmutagen:                      # Per-mutagen settings.\r\n  comparison:                 # Settings of the comparison mutagen.\r\n    enum_bounds: false        # Treat the lowest and highest constant of a defined integer type as its bounds, so v == Lowest isn't mutated to v <= Lowest. Only safe when no value of the type is converted from an arbitrary integer.\r\n\r\nt"]
[0.004069, "o", "hreshold:                    # Quality gates: minimum mutation scores in percent and the most surviving mutants allowed; failing one, gooze exits with code 3. 0 turns a threshold off.\r\n  total: 0                    # Minimum for the score of all mutations.\r\n  average: 0                  # Minimum for the average of the per-file scores.\r\n  file: 0                     # Minimum for the score every file must reach.\r\n  max_survivors: 0            # Most surviving mutants allowed; a --diff run counts the ones on its changed lines.\r\n  diff:                       # Thresholds for --diff runs, scored on the changed lines; they replace the scores above there.\r\n    total: 0                  # Minimum for the changed lines' score.\r\n    average: 0                # Minimum for the average of the changed files' scores.\r\n    file: 0                   # Minimum for the score every changed file must reach.\r\n\r\nreport:                       # Report output settings.\r\n  format: text                # How gooze report view writes "]
[0.004086, "o", "surviving mutants: text, github (workflow annotations on the lines, then the text summary), sarif (a SARIF 2.1.0 log for code scanning), codeclimate (a Code Climate JSON report for GitLab Code Quality; gitlab is the same) or metrics (the score and counts as a GitLab metrics report).\r\n  oci:                        # How gooze report push packages reports for an OCI registry.\r\n    # compat: false           # Push reports with only widely accepted media types (an unknown config and an application/tar+gzip layer), for registries such as GitLab's that reject custom ones. Unset, it is on for registry.gitlab.com and the compat_hosts; true or false sets it for every registry.\r\n    compat_hosts: []          # Registry hosts, and their subdomains, that get compat mode without report.oci.compat (registry.gitlab.com always does).\r\n\r\nlog:                          # Logging settings.\r\n  filename: .gooze.log        # Log file path.\r\n  level: info                 # Log severity: debug, info, warn or error, or a numeric slog"]
[0.004164, "o", " level (-4 debug, 0 info, 4 warn, 8 error).\r\n  verbose: false              # Enable debug-level logging.\r\n  max_size: 10                # Max log size in MiB before rotation.\r\n  max_backups: 3              # Number of rotated log files to retain.\r\n  max_age: 28                 # Days to keep rotated logs.\r\n  compress: true              # Gzip rotated logs.\r\n"]
